     You have to be putting on armor that requires multiple turns
to complete the action, and the nymph (or monkey) has to steal
some other already worn armor which also takes multiple turns.
(Monkeys usually give up if they try to target multi-turn armor,
so this is much more likely to happen with nymphs.)  Most suits
and helms take multiple turns; all gloves and boots do.  Cloaks,
shirts, and shields take a single turn.

     Taking armor off is also susceptible to this bug, but you
won't notice any problem there.  It just won't finish properly,
and you'll end up with the armor still worn and no message about
failing to take it off.  And taking off via 'A' isn't affected,
only via 'T'.  ['A' uses 'occupation' rather than 'afternmv' to
make the hero wait until something has finished before being able
to do something else.]

     Rings take only one turn so aren't susceptible.  I thought
they needed extra turns when wearing gloves, to account for the
time needed to take those off and put back on, but that doesn't
seem to be the case.  Or I'm looking in the wrong place.  Anyway,
rings don't use the 'afternmv' mechanism to do something after
keeping the hero busy for a while, so aren't affected by theft's
use of that same mechanism for multi-turn armor.


